Phase_Timeline: [Estimated duration or time allocation for this phase]

Phase_Deliverables: [List concrete outputs produced by this phase]

Evolution_Mode: [Select: standard, adversarial, quality_diversity, or guided]

Complexity_Score: [Integer 1-10 with breakdown]

Team_Assignment: [Recommend which team should handle this phase]

Testing_Approach: [How to verify this phase is complete]

Quality_Metrics: [Format: "accuracy: X.X | performance: Y | security: [a, b] | compliance: [c, d]"]

Associated_Risks: [List 2-3 risks specific to this time phase]

Success_Dependencies: [What outputs from previous phases are required]

Rationale: [Why this temporal ordering makes sense]
---

IMPORTANT GUIDELINES:
- Provide 3-7 sub-problems representing distinct time phases
- Order MUST reflect chronological sequence
- Each phase should have clear milestones
- Consider natural project phases (planning → foundation → implementation → testing → deployment)
